### Pipeline IAM Role

The GitHub Actions pipeline role **SHALL** be scoped to the minimum permissions required for infrastructure provisioning in the target account. It **SHALL** have a permission boundary that prevents the pipeline from granting itself or other roles permissions beyond the boundary.

```json
{
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {"Federated": "arn:aws:iam::{account}:oidc-provider/token.actions.githubusercontent.com"},
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {
        "token.actions.githubusercontent.com:aud": "sts.amazonaws.com",
        "token.actions.githubusercontent.com:sub": "repo:mygainwell/eap-ref-architecture:ref:refs/heads/main"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

The `sub` condition **SHALL** restrict role assumption to the specific repository and branch, preventing any other GitHub repository from assuming the pipeline role.

